# NexOS process capability policy.
#
# Format:
#   <exec-path-or-basename> <cap|all|none|mask> ...
#
# A matching rule limits the process to the listed capabilities. It never
# grants capabilities the parent process does not already have.
#
# Examples:
#   /cmd/mplay audio
#   doom32 display audio input
#   dbg debug
#   * none

# First tightening pass:
# - unknown executables start with no global process capabilities
# - interactive shell and the multicall toolbox keep authority for now
# - standalone media/UI/test binaries get only their broad device class caps
#
# Note: most /cmd applet names are small scripts that exec /cmd/ush, which
# then runs /cmd/nexbox. Per-applet policy needs argv/action-aware policy later.

/cmd/ush all
ush all
/BOOT/USH32.ELF all
USH.ELF all
USH32.ELF all

/cmd/nexbox all
nexbox all
/cmd/nexbox32s all
nexbox32s all
/BOOT/NEXBOX32.ELF all
/BOOT/NEXBOX32S.ELF all
NEXBOX.ELF all
NEXBOX32.ELF all
NEXBOX32S.ELF all

/cmd/su all
su all
/cmd/sudo all
sudo all

# These multicall aliases control the machine and must retain root power caps.
/cmd/reboot all
reboot all
/cmd/poweroff all
poweroff all

/cmd/doom display audio input
doom display audio input
/cmd/doom32 display audio input
doom32 display audio input
/BOOT/DOOM32.ELF display audio input
DOOM32.ELF display audio input

/cmd/imgview display input
imgview display input
/cmd/guidemo display input
guidemo display input
/cmd/prism display input
prism display input
/cmd/prism32 display input
prism32 display input
/cmd/desktop none
desktop none
/cmd/desktop32 none
desktop32 none
/cmd/prismsmoke none
prismsmoke none
/cmd/prismsmoke32 none
prismsmoke32 none

/cmd/test32 all
test32 all
/BOOT/TEST32.ELF all
TEST32.ELF all

* none
